{"name":"Grey Owl","hex":"#776f67","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"owl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Old Welsh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various birds of prey of the order Strigiformes, families Strigidae and Tytonidae, that are primarily nocturnal and have forward-looking, binocular vision, limited eye movement, and good hearing. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person seen as having owl-like characteristics, especially appearing wise or serious, or being nocturnally active."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grey Owl","blocks":[{"text":"Archibald Stansfeld Belaney, commonly known as Grey Owl, was a popular Canadian writer, public speaker and conservationist. Born an Englishman, he immigrated to Canada and in the latter years of his life, passed as half-Indigenous, falsely claiming he was the son of a Scottish man and an Apache woman. With books, articles and public appearances promoting wilderness conservation, he achieved fame in the 1930s. Shortly after his death in 1938, his real identity as the Englishman Archie Belaney was exposed. He has been called one of the first Canadian \"Pretendians\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Grey_Owl.jpg/330px-Grey_Owl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_Owl","wikidata":"Q1377706"},{"title":"Grey Owl (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Grey Owl is a 1999 biographical film directed by Richard Attenborough and starring Pierce Brosnan in the title-role of the real-life British schoolboy turned Native American trapper Archibald Belaney, known as \"Grey Owl\", and Annie Galipeau as his wife Anahareo, with brief appearances by Graham Greene and others. The screenplay was written by William Nicholson. The film was released on 10 September 1999 in Spain and 15 February 2000 in US. It was the last film made by Largo Entertainment before it went defunct in 1999."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7c/Grey_Owl_%28film%29_cover.jpg/330px-Grey_Owl_%28film%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_Owl_(film)","wikidata":"Q1240641"},{"title":"Owl","blocks":[{"text":"Owls are birds from the order Strigiformes, which includes over 200 species of mostly solitary and nocturnal birds of prey typified by an upright stance, a large, broad head, binocular vision, binaural hearing, sharp talons, and feathers adapted for silent flight. Exceptions include the diurnal northern hawk-owl and the gregarious burrowing owl."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG/330px-Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","wikidata":"Q25222"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Grey_owl_feeding_beaver_a_jelly_roll.jpg/500px-Grey_owl_feeding_beaver_a_jelly_roll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Grey_owl_feeding_beaver_a_jelly_roll.jpg/500px-Grey_owl_feeding_beaver_a_jelly_roll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grey Owl feeding a jelly roll to a beaver","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrey_owl_feeding_beaver_a_jelly_roll.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg/500px-Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg/1280px-Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg/500px-Anahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anahareo holding a beaver","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnahareo_and_a_beaver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/The_Passing_of_the_Last_Frontier_-_first_page.jpg/500px-The_Passing_of_the_Last_Frontier_-_first_page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/The_Passing_of_the_Last_Frontier_-_first_page.jpg/500px-The_Passing_of_the_Last_Frontier_-_first_page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Passing of the Last Frontier\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Passing_of_the_Last_Frontier_-_first_page.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Grey_Owl_and_wife_Anahareo_at_cabin%2C_Lake_Ajawaan%2C_Saskatchewan.jpg/500px-Grey_Owl_and_wife_Anahareo_at_cabin%2C_Lake_Ajawaan%2C_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm